{"name":"Subtle Breeze","hex":"#b5d2d8","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"subtle","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Senses relating to tangible things.\nOf an action or movement: very delicate or slight, and thus barely noticeable; not obvious; inconspicuous, unintrusive.\n\n Having a delicate or fine substance or texture; hence, exquisite, refined.\n Slender, thin.\n Of a substance: finely powdered; also, of particles of a substance: very fine or small.\n Of weight: after the tare (“weight of an empty container”) has been subtracted; net.","Of an action or movement: very delicate or slight, and thus barely noticeable; not obvious; inconspicuous, unintrusive."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["People or things that are subtle (adjective sense) as a class."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/subtle"},{"term":"breeze","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A light, gentle wind.","Any activity that is easy, not testing or difficult."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To move casually, in a carefree manner.","To blow gently."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/breeze"}],"entries":[],"images":[],"sounds":{"subtle":[{"type":"audio/ogg; codecs=\"vorbis\"","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/7/7c/En-us-subtle.ogg?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=original"},{"type":"audio/mpeg","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/7/7c/En-us-subtle.ogg/En-us-subtle.ogg.mp3"},{"type":"audio/wav","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/2/20/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Naomi_Persephone_Amethyst_%28NaomiAmethyst%29-subtle.wav?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=original"},{"type":"audio/mpeg","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/2/20/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Naomi_Persephone_Amethyst_%28NaomiAmethyst%29-subtle.wav/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Naomi_Persephone_Amethyst_%28NaomiAmethyst%29-subtle.wav.mp3"},{"type"